  "thesis": "A 31.5% rally, a 5.9% giveback, and a Congress that wants answers: Huang is back, but the questions that ousted him are not settled.",
  "lede": "NVIDIA's board unanimously reinstated Jensen Huang as President, CEO and director on Nov 23, citing input from senior levels of the US government. NVDA closed Monday at $165.05, up 31.5%, adding about $950 billion; on Tuesday it gave back 5.9% to $155.38 and the chip index fell 7.9%, on profit-taking and the political and regulatory risk still hanging over the company. In 357 verified quotes from 216 voices, opposition outnumbers support about two to one. None of the 36 members of Congress on record supports the move, from Sanders and Van Hollen to Rick Scott, Britt and Cotton; the FT called it \"a triumph of money over morals\" and the WSJ editorial board \"a political bailout.\" The administration doubled down: Trump said a pardon is \"always an option,\" and Attorney General Todd Blanche asked what Huang would have been investigated for. Abroad, Netanyahu welcomed it, China's foreign ministry had \"no comment,\" and Singapore's Lawrence Wong said \"So be it.\" Huang's Dec 3 testimony and the board's investigation decide what comes next.",
